 "name": "Museum Facades and Emotional Experience (Beijing Olympic Park): PAD Scale",
 "description": "Faithful replication of Zhang et al. (2025), Buildings 15:57. Participants look at three photographs of museum facades in the Beijing Olympic Park Museum Group (Museum of the Communist Party of China, Chinese Traditional Culture Museum, China Science and Technology Museum), shown one at a time in random order and self-paced. They then rate how the pictures made them feel on the 12-item simplified Chinese PAD scale (pleasure, arousal, dominance; 9-point semantic differential, −4 to +4, adjective pairs from the paper's Table 3) and rate their emotional experience of 11 environmental characteristics (material, color, natural elements, form and structure, privacy, diversity, sociability, territoriality, playability, uniqueness, changeability; 1–7). Gender and major (design-related or not) are asked first. Stimuli: the paper's own processed photographs (Figure 4; taken 5 June 2023, pedestrians and traffic lights erased and sky tone unified in Adobe Photoshop 2019), cropped from the CC BY 4.0 article; credited on the page and removed if the authors object. Differences from the original study: (1) the paper recorded eye movements with a Tobii Pro Fusion eye tracker in a lab; this template records only viewing time per picture; (2) the three operation-practice pictures are left out; (3) the photographs come from the published figure (about 730 × 410 px) instead of the 2560 × 1440 originals; (4) English wording of the PAD adjective pairs follows the paper's English table, not the Chinese questionnaire.",
